   "text": "# FEB 20 – TO DOs & KYRIAN’S ADVICE\n\n## Context (Google Meet – Feb 20)\n\nKyrian needed confirmation on the real state of the website that Jonathan was expected to complete on Feb 19.\n\nMultiple issues surfaced. Jonathan identified excessive AI-generated content inside YAML files, including placeholders and mock values.\n\nDecision:\n\n* Rebuild the website from scratch.\n* Reuse only the last meaningful commit from Kyrian.\n* Exclude placeholders and unverifiable data.\n\nKyrian accepted the reset, but emphasized:\n\n* The site was due yesterday.\n* Time is critical.\n* Delivery must happen today (Feb 20).\n\n---\n\n## Kyrian’s Instructions After Reviewing the Site\n\n### 1. CTAs (Nice to Have, but High Priority Quality)\n\n* Forms (email, contact, WhatsApp).\n* Use Erebus AI agent phone number.\n* Never use personal numbers.\n* Always test CTAs thoroughly.\n\n  * A broken form is worse than no form.\n\n### 2. Data Integrity\n\n* No placeholder values.\n* No mock statistics.\n* No fake clients.\n* If unverifiable → remove.\n* Focus on high-quality product presentation.\n\n### 3. Simplicity Over Fragility\n\n* Prefer JSON loaders over YAML if type issues appear.\n* Reduce structural complexity.\n* Avoid unnecessary abstractions.\n\n### 4. Deployment Discipline\n\n* Never push unfinished projects.\n* Local validation first.\n* Production only after verification.\n\n### 5. Messaging & Positioning\n\n* Sell AI **ACCELERATION**, not vague “efficiency”.\n* Core motto:\n\n  > Stop doing robots’ work. Make the robots do the human job.\n* Wizard-style branding (light inspiration only):\n\n  * “Casting spells”\n  * “Selling scrolls”\n* Styling is last priority.\n\n### 6. Repository Hygiene\n\n* Use opencode for full-repo visibility.\n* Reorganize aggressively.\n* Abstract only when justified.\n* Remove illogical integrations.\n* Keep documentation aligned with actual code state.\n\n---\n\n# Implementation Loop\n\nGeneral framework. The only non-negotiable rule: **Follow John’s CI/CD.**\nGoal: Zero slop. Professional-grade output only.\n\nWe operate under TDD.\n\n---\n\n## 0. TDD (Foundational Rule)\n\nShift quality left.\nPrevent QA debt instead of fixing it later.\n\nFocus:\n\n* Test types\n* Coverage scope\n* Target clarity\n* Explicit reasoning for each test\n\nSlower upfront. Superior outcome.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Verify\n\nBefore committing:\n\n* Validate staged changes.\n* Detect hallucinated AI content.\n* Remove fake metrics and invented clients.\n* No fabricated business claims.\n\nProfessionalism > speed.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Report\n\n* Critique aggressively.\n* Identify abstraction leaks.\n* Reorganize structure.\n* Produce Markdown audit report.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Epics & Tasks\n\nFrom the report:\n\n* Build checklist.\n* Keep tasks atomic.\n* No overengineering.\n* No placeholders.\n* No mock data.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Implementation (Controlled)\n\n* Enforce John’s CI/CD.\n* Respect .cursor settings.\n* Cyclomatic control in core features.\n* Include unit tests always.\n* Avoid DRY-runs and smoke tests unless strictly necessary.\n* Do not finish all epic tasks in one sweep.\n* Validate incrementally.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Feature Addition (After Tests Exist)\n\nOnly after:\n\n* Tests are written.\n* Tests are documented.\n\nThen:\n\n* Implement feature code.\n\nStrict TDD.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Test Pipeline Update\n\n* Extend automation harness.\n* Integrate feature into CI.\n* Avoid manual debt.\n* Accelerate integration from day one.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Documentation Update\n\n* Update docs with every major change.\n* Prefer parallel opencode agent for automatic doc updates.\n* Documentation must reflect real state.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Feedback Loops\n\nJohn’s CI/CD provides modular quality gates.\n\nRun:\n1 → 7 continuously\nFeed results back\nTighten quality\nReduce entropy\n\n---\n\n# Deadline Today (February 20).\n\n* **Urgency:** Must be finished within the first few hours following the meeting.\n\nRationale:\n* The issues discovered should have been communicated immediately and tested thoroughly, rather than leaving an agent to run blindly on an automated CI/CD loop expecting perfection. Time is highly valuable right now.\n* Blind trust in automated loops is not acceptable as well as manual fixing issues or performing development itself.\n\nFinal objective:\n\n* Clean rebuild.\n* No hallucinated content.\n* Fully validated.\n* Production-ready within hours.\n* Issues communication must happen immediately.",
